            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery narrowing after aortic root reconstruction with resorcin-formalin glue.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1701-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Severe stenosis of right and left main coronary artery ostia developed after aortic root reconstruction with gelatin-resorcin-formol glue for correction of acute type A aortic dissection. Surgical treatment of this condition required grafting of the right and left anterior descending arteries with bilateral mammary arteries on the beating heart.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
